# Houzz Project Tracker — Category Taxonomy & Import Guard

**Canonical doc:** `Docs/CLEANUP_HISTORY.md` (May 27, 2026 taxonomy supersedes Clipper whitelist; commit `12afe16` on GitHub).

**Do not use raw Houzz Project Tracker or Outgoing PO reports without this context.** April 2026 large import + May 27 cleanup fixed categories, types, expense flags, and rooms. Re-imports that overwrite guarded fields bring bad data back.

## Root cause (tracker exports are dirty)

- Wrong categories: `Fabric  + Trim`, `Appliances  & Plumbing`, granular appliance names, rooms as categories (`LIGHTING`, `TV`, `Inventory`, names)
- Services/expenses in Category column: Freight, Expense, Prepaid Tax, Time Billing without `expenseType`
- Garbage: `cr`, blank, `Uncategorized` (~222 rows in bad import sample)
- Trailing whitespace → duplicate distinct values (`Fabric & Trim` vs `Fabric & Trim `)

## CCH canonical product categories (21)

Lighting · Mirrors & Accessories · Accessories · **Furniture & Upholstery** · Fabric & Trim · **Cabinet Hardware** · **Window Hardware** · Bedding & Pillows · **Custom Pillows & Bedding** (not "Custom Bedding and Pillows") · **Custom Window Treatments** (not "Custom Window Coverings") · Windows · Wall · Wall Covering · Appliances & Plumbing · Floor Covering · **Rugs** · Stone & Tile · Cabinets · Florals · Art · Architectural

## Expense/service (NOT product categories)

Set `expenseType` + `taxable: false`:

- **Freight** → `expenseType: 'freight'`
- **Labor** → `expenseType: 'service'`
- **Expense** / **Prepaid Tax** → `expenseType: 'expense'`
- **Custom Upholstery** → labor-only (`service`); if not labor, remap to **Furniture & Upholstery**

## Import-time rules (all Houzz import paths)

1. **Trim** leading/trailing whitespace on every `category` (and related) write.
2. **Keyword scan** on title + description + vendor + sku:
   - `\bfreight\b` → Freight, expenseType=freight, taxable=No
   - `\blabor\b|\binstall\b|\breupholster\b|\btailor\b|\bfabricat\b` → Labor, expenseType=service, taxable=No
3. **Apply remap table** in `CLEANUP_HISTORY.md` § "May 27, 2026 — CCH Canonical Category Taxonomy".
4. Set **`_taxonomyV: "2026-05-27"`** on cleaned docs.
5. **Re-Import Guard Rules** (top of `CLEANUP_HISTORY.md`): never overwrite cleaned `category`, `expenseType`, `taxable`, Firebase `imageUrl`, or hand-curated `room`. Fill-empty-only when `_categoryFixedAt` / `_taxableFixedAt` / protected `source` is set.

## Code touchpoints

- `import-houzz-data.js`
- `platform/index.html` — `_houzzImportMapInvoiceLine()` and related Houzz import
- Any script touching `products/` or `productLibrary/` categories
- PO audits: outgoing report totals ≠ tracker categories; use correct source per job (tracker vs outgoing xlsx)

## Reference files (New Houzz reports folder)

- Bad sample: `STUDIO_PRODUCTS_IMPORT BAD REPORT BAD CATEGORIES.csv`
- Cleaned: `STUDIO_PRODUCTS_IMPORT_CLEANED_BY_CLAUDE_May27.csv`, `STUDIO_PRODUCTS_IMPORT_CLEANED_v4_FINAL_May27.csv`

## Agent-produced spreadsheets (Cynthia rule)

Never overwrite Cynthia's working XLSX/CSV. Use distinct names:

- `*_BY_CLAUDE_<descriptor>_<date>.xlsx` (or `.csv`)
- Example fix: `PO_STUBS_AUDIT_BY_CLAUDE_2026-05-27.xlsx` not `PO_STUBS_AUDIT_2026-05-27.xlsx`

Avoids Excel + Dropbox lock conflicts when agents read files.

## PO / payment work (separate from category cleanup)

- `restore-po-vendors-from-tracker.js` = legacy **Cloud** tracker vendors only; does **not** fix New Houzz outgoing PO payment multipliers, missing POs, or stub totals.
- `audit-new-houzz-outgoing.js` = read-only vs Outgoing Transactions xlsx.
- Payment 2×–7× issues need dedupe + replace-not-append sync fixes — not a blind re-import.
